  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">1. `sprk_objectrecordname` exists live under the Spaarke publisher in SpaarkeCore, verified by describe() before the PCF deployed. `NoAccessListReader.RowSelect` is unchanged (diff). The schema doc records the column as a display snapshot, not a key.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">2. Picker: choosing a project, matter or work assignment writes `sprk_objectrecordtype` (that type's `sprk_recordtype_ref` row), `sprk_objectrecordid` (lowercase, unbraced GUID) and `sprk_objectrecordname` together, and clears `sprk_objectorganization`. A failed record-type resolution writes none of them and shows an inline error. Only the step-1-verified types are offered. The control renders read-only when disabled. Each case is covered by a component test.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">3. An entry created through the picker for record R walls a contact named as subject: the SPA/Teams plane denies that contact on R after save (live). This proves the stored id matches the reader's filter (`NoAccessListReader.cs:221-222`).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">4. The entry form refuses to save, with a form notification naming the problem, when it has zero or more than one subject, zero objects, both object forms, a half record pair, or an object record id that is not a GUID. Choosing an organization clears the record pair and name. A well-formed entry saves, and 143's post-save enforce call still runs and shows its notice. Exactly one form library is registered on the sprk_noaccessentry main form besides `sprk_/scripts/bff_auth.js`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">5. Quick create is off for sprk_noaccessentry. "+ New" on each of the three subgrids opens the main form with the right lookup prefilled (object organization, subject organization or subject contact).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">6. The Organization form shows the NO ACCESS section on the SYSTEM ACCESS / MEMBERS tab with the two subgrids and their columns; the Contact form shows its section with one subgrid. Reason is not a subgrid column. Every subgrid lists active entries only.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">7. The closed set of views exists with the stated columns. "Incomplete Entries — deny nothing" lists exactly the malformed rows (live, seeded through the Web API as an access administrator, since the form refuses them: one row with two subjects, one with no object, one with a half record pair; all three appear, and a well-formed row does not; then deactivate the seeded rows). Built only after escalation (h) clears. The lookup view shows subject and object.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">8. The site map of the app chosen in step 1 has a "No Access Entries" subarea opening "Active No Access Entries". Under O2's recommendation, a user without Read does not see it.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">9. O2 applied as answered (accepted 2026-10-01), with before/after privileges recorded for each role. Under the accepted recommendation:
- a non-administrator test user cannot open an entry, cannot create one, and a Web API read of `sprk_noaccessentries` is refused with a privilege error (not a 200 with an empty list);
- an access-administrator test user can create, read, update and deactivate entries but not delete them;
- the BFF deny read still denies a walled contact on the SPA plane (live).
Per constraint "no false empty", a user without Read never sees an empty NO ACCESS grid.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">10. N5 on the new form, live. An entry whose author holds Write on record R is enforced on R. An organization wall whose author lacks Write on some covered records shows the per-record "not enforced" outcome for exactly those records, in the notice and (if 143 persists it) on the form and the view.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">11. MANUAL live gate on spaarkedev1, using existing non-admin test users in their current BUs, with screenshots recorded:
(i) an access administrator opens an Organization, adds an ethical wall naming a contact through "Ethical walls on this organization", and the contact is then denied on a matter referencing that organization;
(ii) the same administrator adds the organization as a denied subject against a specific project through the picker;
(iii) adds a contact as denied from the Contact form;
(iv) opens "Active No Access Entries" from the site map and sees all three entries with readable object names (no raw GUIDs);
(v) a non-administrator user opening the same Organization sees no entries and no empty NO ACCESS grid;
(vi) dark mode per the ui-tests.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">12. Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named in criteria 2, 4, 5, 7 and 9 (type resolution failure, mutually exclusive objects, GUID normalization, malformed shapes, prefill per subgrid, role negatives). No criterion is met by a test that only asserts a mock was called with arguments the test itself supplied. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the notes. No ADR-038-banned test shapes. `npm run build:prod` succeeds and the picker's jest suite is green. No BFF change, no plugin, no flow. The entity-schema.md organization-level section and the §5 registry row are written.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Add an ethical wall from the Organization form">
      <url>https://{org}.crm.dynamics.com/main.aspx?appid={app-id}&amp;pagetype=entityrecord&amp;etn=sprk_organization&amp;id={organization-id}</url>
      <steps>
        <step>Sign in as the access-administrator test user (an existing non-admin test user, in its current BU, given the new "Spaarke Access Administrator" role per O2)</step>
        <step>Open the tab with SYSTEM ACCESS and MEMBERS; locate the NO ACCESS section</step>
        <step>Click "+ New" on "Ethical walls on this organization"; verify Object Organization is prefilled; choose a Subject Contact; enter a Reason; save</step>
        <step>Check the browser console for errors</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The main form (not a quick create) opened with the object prefilled; the save succeeded; 143's enforcement notice appeared; the subgrid lists the new entry; no console errors.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Pick an object record instead of typing a GUID">
      <steps>
        <step>From "This organization denied", click "+ New"</step>
        <step>In the Object section, use the record picker: choose type Matter, then pick a matter in the lookup pane</step>
        <step>Save; open "Active No Access Entries"</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The picker offers only Project, Matter and Work Assignment (or the step-1-verified set); the chosen matter shows as a chip; Object Organization is cleared; the view shows the matter's name, not a GUID.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Malformed entry is refused">
      <steps>
        <step>Create an entry with both a Subject Contact and a Subject Organization; try to save</step>
        <step>Create an entry with no object; try to save</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Each save is blocked with a form notification naming the problem; nothing is created.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Contact form NO ACCESS section">
      <url>https://{org}.crm.dynamics.com/main.aspx?appid={app-id}&amp;pagetype=entityrecord&amp;etn=contact&amp;id={contact-id}</url>
      <steps>
        <step>As the access administrator, open a Contact; use "+ New" on "This contact denied"; pick a project as the object; save</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The entry is created with the contact prefilled and appears in the subgrid.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Non-administrator sees no false empty grid">
      <steps>
        <step>Sign in as an existing non-administrator test user; open the same Organization</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>No entries are visible and no empty NO ACCESS grid suggests that nobody is denied (the section is hidden or shows a permission message).</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Dark Mode Compliance (ADR-021)">
      <steps>
        <step>Toggle dark mode; open an entry with a picked object record</step>
        <step>Verify the picker's chip, button and error text adapt (no hard-coded colours; icons use currentColor)</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>All picker colours use Fluent v9 semantic tokens.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <notes>Owner round 3b (session27-owner-decisions-and-research.md:79-83) and disposition row 5 + O2 (session27-ux-research-ethical-wall-secure.md:71, :75-76). Coordination the orchestrator must act on:
- 143's form dependency is absorbed here. 143 keeps ownership of the enforce endpoint, its post-save call and the persisted N5 outcome; this task extends 143's form library with the OnSave check, and keeps it registered.
- 143 ↔ 154 is a two-way PARTIAL dependency: 154 needs 143's server and schema steps; 143's form steps and live gate need 154's form. TASK-INDEX should show 154's dep on 143 as "143 (server + schema steps)" and 143's on 154 as "154 (form steps only)", or the two block each other.
- 064's question to the orchestrator (do 154's subgrids need to read through 064's routes once O2 lands?) is answered here: no — the sections serve access administrators, who keep table Read; everyone else gets 153's banner.
- Schema-doc drift to fix with 143: Business Rule 1 (`entity-schema.md:105-110`) says the reader excludes rows with neither or both SUBJECT fields, but today's reader checks only the object shape (`NoAccessListReader.cs:390-406`); 143 criterion 1 closes it.
- 064's endpoints are the BFF write path. Its entry validation and the reader's malformed-row rule are the server-side owners of the entry shape (new §5 registry row).
- 153 registers its banner library on the Organization and Contact forms after this task, and its copy points at the NO ACCESS section.
- If escalation (d) confirms per-child objects are evaluated nowhere, the orchestrator decides whether to raise a server task.
The organization-level answer the owner asked for lands in entity-schema.md (step 7) and should be quoted back to the owner.</notes>

