  <amendments date="2026-10-05" source="owner round 59, 2026-10-05, BINDING (notes/session27-owner-decisions-and-research.md, 'Owner round 59'; evidence: notes/batch5-scope-review-2026-10-05.md, row 154)">
    <verdict>KEEP, REDUCED (owner round 59 items 4 and 8). Runs FIRST in batch 5: it closes a class (a) fail-open defect (a record id typed with braces creates a wall that walls nothing) and a disclosure defect (every core user reads every Reason).</verdict>
    <amendment n="1" title="Scope">Entry form with all fields and both scripts registered (143's on-save enforcement is not registered on any form today). A save-time id check in the existing sprk_noaccessentry_postsave.js normalises and refuses a non-canonical sprk_objectrecordid. Server half: the reader's existing malformed-row rule rejects a non-canonical id (NoAccessListReader.cs:596 / :330), so an entry written by Web API or import shows as malformed instead of silently walling nothing. Also: quick-create off; 3 subgrids; one view; one menu entry (escalation c: which app); O2 (remove Read from Spaarke Core User, Read/Write for the access-administrator role); doc fixes (entity-schema.md:104, :139, :237).</amendment>
    <amendment n="2" title="Record picker: REUSE, do not build">Kept, because pasting record GUIDs is not usable and is how the silent-wall defect arises. Reuse the EXISTING polymorphic record picker (RegardingResolver / PolymorphicPicker, as the filing forms use it). Do NOT build the new ObjectRecordPicker PCF. The display-name column sprk_objectrecordname is kept ONLY if the picker cannot show the record without it.</amendment>
    <amendment n="3" title="Cut">The ObjectRecordPicker PCF; the 'Incomplete Entries' view and its seed test; the extra views; sprk_objectrecordname unless the picker needs it.</amendment>
    <amendment n="4" title="Dependencies">No longer depends on 064: the deny-list add/remove endpoints it needed are cut, and 154 now runs before 064 (064 soft-depends on 154's id normalisation). Depends on 143 (server work merged).</amendment>
  </amendments>
